        <h2>JavaScript in the page</h2>
        <p>
            The interface around the engine is React, bundled into the script
            your browser downloads — so that file is a binary distribution of
            these packages in exactly the way the <code>.wasm</code> is of the
            crates below. They are npm packages rather than Cargo dependencies,
            so <code>cargo about</code> cannot see them and they are listed here
            by hand, the same way the models are. The bundler does extract
            React's own banners into a <code>.js.LICENSE.txt</code> file beside
            the bundle, but those banners only point at a LICENSE file in
            React's source tree that is not shipped — the licence text itself is
            below.
        </p>
        <p>
            Everything else in <code>package.json</code> is a build-time
            dependency — bundler, compiler, test runner — and none of it ships
            any code to your browser, so none of it is listed here.
        </p>
